  "name": "simple-sexp",
  "description": "A minimalist implementation of symbolic expression (S-expression) parsing and serialization leveraging algebraic data types in an early dialect of Rust. It features a recursive descent parser and a peekable character-based lexer to transform string inputs into nested list structures and atomic primitives. The library provides a foundational data model and formatter for Lisp-like data interchange and symbolic computation.",
